{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And she called his name Shelah, and he was in Keziv, etc.</b> This means: therefore she called his name Shelah, because she ceased from giving birth, for the term שלה and the term כזיב are one, as it is written: one says ״אל תכזב בשפחתך״ and another writes ״אל תשלה בי״, and כזיב is a term of cessation, as in ״וכמוצא מים אשר לא יכזבו מימיו״. And from my master, z\"l, I heard that this was their custom: he would name the first son and she would name the second son. If so, by right Judah should have named the third. But she named him, as it is written ותקרא. Therefore it was necessary to state that Judah was in Keziv when she gave birth to him, and was not present at that event to name him. Keziv is a place name."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:06:40.674638300Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}